What the tests establish:

| Test | Property |
|---|---|
| `TestCMACRFC4493Vectors` | CMAC matches NIST/RFC 4493 vectors. |
| `TestGHASHMatchesStdlib` | Our independent `GF(2¹²⁸)`/GHASH matches `crypto/cipher` GCM tags (200 random cases), validating the salamander solver. |
| `TestRoundTripSingleKey` | Round trip for plaintext lengths 0–4096, correct ring index. |
| `TestDuplicateKeysAreNotAmbiguous` | Repeated identical keys are one key. |
| `TestWrongRingRejected` | Non-holding ring → `ErrNoMatch`. |
| `TestTamperRejected` | Flipping every byte is rejected. |
| `TestPlainGCMIsNotKeyCommitting` | Positive control: one salamander verifies under two keys, two different plaintexts. |
| `TestCommittedVariantBoundsAcceptedSet` | Core: committed envelope around a genuine salamander has `|Acc| ∈ {0,1}`, never 2. |
| `TestAcceptedSetAtMostOneOnMutations` | Every byte mutation keeps `|Acc| ≤ 1`. |
| `TestNonceMisuseSafety` | Nonce reuse gives different `synthNonce`, breaks `C1⊕C2=P1⊕P2`. |
| `TestAmbiguousSplitEncoding` | Length-prefix prevents SIV-input collisions. |
| `TestTagSizesAndForgery` | 128-bit tags; random tags rejected. |
| `FuzzAcceptedSetAtMostOne` | Arbitrary adversarial envelopes keep `|Acc| ≤ 1`, no panics. |

**Constant-time:** `DecryptCommitted` uses `crypto/subtle.ConstantTimeCompare` for the commitment; GCM's `Open` uses `subtle.ConstantTimeCompare` internally (confirmed in `crypto/internal/fips140/aes/gcm/`). No byte-wise short-circuit.

**Two subtle bugs caught and fixed during development:** (1) the embedded salamander must collide on the *derived* `kEnc` subkeys, not the master keys; (2) naive `CMAC(kMac, nonce‖ad‖pt)` is non-injective (`(ad="a",pt="bc")` ≡ `(ad="ab",pt="c")`), so the SIV input is length-prefixed.
